          "id": "SP_TEREBELLUM_CINCTUM_K_MARTIN_1916",
          "name": "Terebellum cinctum K.Martin, 1916",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Terebellum",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The shell is smooth and narrow, with a blunt teleoconch. There is a carina above the defined suture, with distinct incised spiral lines being the only sculpture on the teleoconch. The basal sculpture is not known. The labial callus is moderately developed.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:8979840",
          "authorship": "K.Martin",
          "yearPublished": "1916",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_TEREBELLUM_DELICATUM_KURODA_KAWAMOTO_1956",
          "name": "Terebellum delicatum Kuroda & Kawamoto, 1956",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Terebellum",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The shell is smooth, ovately rotund and quadrate at the base. The sutures are well-developed, and the labrum is protocyrt. The spire is blunt, and the aperture extends for three-quarters the length of the shell. There is a distinctive central axial mid-columella ridge that may not be evident in subadults. The species lacks the anterior lip marginal black line at maturity. The shell background colour is usually tan with circular white spotting, with a single dark smaller spot within each larger white one such that their circumferences touch, resulting in a white crescent shape partially surrounding the darker spot (Maxwell et al. 2018 b).",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:7727915",
          "authorship": "Kuroda & Kawamoto",
          "yearPublished": "1956",
          "children": []
        },
