          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Paraseraphs",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The shell is smooth and slender, with a protoconch of 11 / 2 to 13 / 4 whorls. The teleoconch has 21 / 2 to 3 whorls. The labial callus is well-developed and the labrum is not thickened. The posterior canal is antispirally bent and does not extend to the apex. The columella is basally bent backward. The labrum does not reach the base of the columella.",
