          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Paraseraphs",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "The shell is smooth and slender, with a high, acute apex thinly covered with shell matrix. The posterior canal is mostly straight, running antispirally towards the apex and reflected at termination. The teleoconch has four whorls. The labial callus is well-developed and the labrum is not thickened. The columella is basally bent backward. The labrum does not reach the base of the columella.",
